<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated Info.plist by the Tauri CLI. Keep it to keys
  Tauri does not already set — overwriting the version or the bundle id
  from here fights the build rather than extending it.

  ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption answers Apple's export-compliance question
  at upload time instead of leaving it for someone to click. Without it,
  App Store Connect refuses the submission with "This build is missing
  export compliance information", which is what happened to the Mac 1.0.1
  upload on 2026-09-23 — the iOS target has carried this key all along, so
  only the Mac build ever asked.

  `false` is the same answer the iOS target gives, and for the same
  reason recorded in apps/ios/store/listing.md: the only cryptography here
  is HTTPS and PDF password encryption, both exempt. If the app ever adds
  encryption of its own beyond that, this key is where the lie would
  start — revisit it rather than leaving it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
